    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        366,
        815,
        1524,
        1036
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, in New York City, where ethnic and racial diversity are appreciated and valued by our inhabitants, it is recognized that bias incidents and other acts motivated by hatred or prejudice are deplorable not only because of the terrible toll they exact from their victims, but also because they undermine the cohesion and tolerance that are necessary in our pluralistic society; and",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.2493,
          "min": -1.3544
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 71,
          "mean": -0.002,
          "min": -0.1436
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 48118,
        "area_px": 260960,
        "density": 0.18439,
        "chars": 386,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 8.02
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        366,
        1071,
        1527,
        1201
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "WHEREAS, it is incumbent on the government of New York City to take all reasonable efforts to prevent bias incidents and community tensions, and to ameliorate their effects when they occur.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2296,
          "min": -1.2447
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0001
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 38,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0013
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 24650,
        "area_px": 153008,
        "density": 0.1611,
        "chars": 189,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 7.67
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        366,
        1237,
        1507,
        1299
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "By the power vested in me as Mayor of the City of New York, it is hereby ordered:",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2345,
          "min": -1.2631
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0264,
          "min": -0.0264
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 20,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.001
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 9376,
        "area_px": 72324,
        "density": 0.12964,
        "chars": 81,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 8.64
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        366,
        1335,
        1548,
        1529
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 1. **Committee Established.** In order to provide broader service to the public and to allay concern about occurrences that may develop into bias incidents, a \"Bias Response Coordinating Committee\" is hereby established. The Committee will be guided in its activities by the Mayor's Bias Response Plan, which is promulgated with this Order.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2195,
          "min": -1.1734
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0032,
          "min": -0.0032
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 71,
          "mean": -0.0091,
          "min": -0.4355
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 45123,
        "area_px": 228928,
        "density": 0.19711,
        "chars": 348,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 7.71
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        368,
        1565,
        1548,
        1885
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "Section 2. **Responsibility.** The Bias Response Coordinating Committee will be responsible for inquiring into bias related criminal and non-criminal bias occurrences that may stimulate additional incidents, or that may escalate community concern, unrest or disruption. Its mission is to ascertain causes for concern, utilize City resources to abate those concerns, communicate information to affected government agencies and public officials, and perform whatever services are necessary to promote public confidence and order.",
      "logprob_stats": {
